**Eating disorders** are **serious mental illnesses** where a person uses controlling food, eating or exercise to cope with difficult feelings or situations. They can seriously affect physical health. With the right support, **people can and do recover**.

## Types of eating disorder

- **Anorexia nervosa:** trying to keep weight as low as possible by eating very little, exercising a lot, or both
- **Bulimia nervosa:** eating a lot of food in a short time (bingeing), then trying to get rid of it, for example by making yourself sick or using laxatives
- **Binge eating disorder:** regularly eating large amounts of food while feeling out of control, without getting rid of it afterwards
- **ARFID** (avoidant restrictive food intake disorder): avoiding certain foods or limiting how much you eat, for example because of fears or sensory issues, not because of body image
- **OSFED** (other specified feeding or eating disorder): when symptoms do not fit exactly into one of the other types. It is just as serious

## Warning signs

- spending a lot of time **worrying about food, weight or body shape**
- **avoiding eating** with others
- **strict rules** or rituals around food
- **eating very little** or **eating large amounts** in secret
- going to the toilet straight after meals
- **exercising a lot**
- changes in **mood**, such as being anxious, low or irritable
- physical signs such as **dizziness, feeling cold**, missed periods or tooth damage

## Getting help

- see your **GP** as soon as possible. Early treatment makes recovery more likely
- if you are worried about someone, gently encourage them to get help
- **Beat** offers free helplines and online support

{% callout type="danger" title="Get urgent help if" %}
You or someone you know **faints**, has **chest pain**, a **very fast or irregular heartbeat**, is **very weak or confused**, or has been **vomiting a lot**. Go to A&E or call **999**. Eating disorders can cause dangerous changes to the body.
{% /callout %}

See [eating disorder treatment](/conditions/mental-health/eating-disorders/treatment/).
